---
import "../styles/global.css";
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <title>ALPS Foundation — ethics charter (draft)</title>
  </head>
  <body class="guide-page">
    <main class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 py-20 md:py-28">
      <p class="mb-10 rounded-sm border border-rule bg-paper-alt p-4 text-sm text-ink-soft">
        <span class="mb-1 block text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-soft/80">
          Draft — not linked from the site, for review only
        </span>
        English translation of the French v0.3 draft, scoped to conduct only. Still pending a
        native-speaker / legal pass before this is public.
      </p>

      <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-soft">ALPS Foundation</p>
      <h1 class="mb-4 text-4xl font-black leading-tight tracking-tight md:text-5xl">Ethics charter</h1>
      <p class="mb-10 text-lg text-ink">
        The code of conduct that governs how ALPS events, teaching, and research are run.
      </p>

      <div class="mb-12 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 rounded-sm border border-rule p-5">
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft">
          This charter covers conduct only. For our mission, vision, and values, see our manifesto.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/manifesto-draft"
          class="whitespace-nowrap border-b border-ink text-sm font-semibold text-ink hover:border-ink-soft hover:text-ink-soft"
        >
          Read the manifesto →
        </a>
      </div>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="mb-4 border-b border-rule pb-2 text-xl font-semibold">Our values</h2>
        <ul class="divide-y divide-rule text-ink-soft">
          <li class="py-3">Non-violence, compassion, wisdom.</li>
          <li class="py-3">Freedom of belief.</li>
          <li class="py-3">
            Respect for every person's dignity: a safe, caring environment and equal opportunity for
            everyone.
          </li>
          <li class="py-3">
            Accountability of organisers and teachers: leading by example, scientific rigour, listening,
            respect for free will, no abuse of authority.
          </li>
          <li class="py-3">Honest, kind speech: no lies, slander, rumours, or hurtful words.</li>
          <li class="py-3">
            Interdependence and harmony within ALPS: cooperation, empathy, solidarity, non-violent
            conflict resolution.
          </li>
          <li class="py-3">
            Compliance: the consumption and trafficking of narcotics are not permitted at ALPS events.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="mb-4 border-b border-rule pb-2 text-xl font-semibold">Behaviours we do not accept</h2>
        <ul class="divide-y divide-rule text-ink-soft">
          <li class="py-3">Any form of abuse — physical, psychological, economic, sexual, or institutional.</li>
          <li class="py-3">Emotional or spiritual manipulation.</li>
          <li class="py-3">Exploiting participants' vulnerability.</li>
          <li class="py-3">Harassment, intimidation, moral violence.</li>
          <li class="py-3">Spreading rumours or lies.</li>
          <li class="py-3">Consumption or trafficking of narcotics at ALPS events.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="mb-4 border-b border-rule pb-2 text-xl font-semibold">Reporting &amp; complaint procedure</h2>
        <ul class="divide-y divide-rule text-ink-soft">
          <li class="py-3">Designated trusted contacts.</li>
          <li class="py-3">A clear, accessible, confidential procedure.</li>
          <li class="py-3">Mediation, internal inquiry, or external recourse where needed.</li>
          <li class="py-3">Protection for anyone reporting abuse.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="mb-4 border-b border-rule pb-2 text-xl font-semibold">Governance &amp; review</h2>
        <ul class="divide-y divide-rule text-ink-soft">
          <li class="py-3">An independent ethics committee.</li>
          <li class="py-3">Regular review of the charter.</li>
          <li class="py-3">Published and posted at conference venues.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <div class="mb-12 rounded-sm border border-rule p-5">
        <p class="mb-2 text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-soft/80">
          Note — the events-vs-access distinction
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft">
          The compliance clause above concerns official ALPS events and teaching activities
          specifically. It is separate from — and does not affect — ALPS's clinical work advising
          practitioners on legal, medically supervised access to psychedelic-assisted therapy, which
          sits outside event conduct and is governed by Swiss medical regulation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <footer class="border-t border-rule pt-8 text-xs text-ink-soft/80">
        <p>
          Draft prepared from the ALPS Task List item "Charter / One-Pager" and its discussion thread,
          20 May – 19 July 2026. Source: Drive doc
          "2026-07-19_Charte-éthique-ALPS-Foundation_FR_v0.3.docx" (v0.3). Mission, vision, and
          activities live separately on the manifesto draft.
        </p>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
